      "rev_n_1_37c1f6_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_37c1f6_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_37c1f6",
        "thought_text": "Sort both Physics and Informatics cups by significance in descending order. This allows us to greedily select the most significant cups while respecting the width constraint.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794531809.543645
      },
      "rev_n_2_083e8a_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_083e8a_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_083e8a",
        "thought_text": "Use dynamic programming to compute the maximum significance for each possible width from 0 to d. For each subject, maintain a prefix sum of significances and another for widths. This allows for efficient querying of the maximum significance for any given width.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794531809.5436661
      },
      "rev_n_3_7821a1_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_7821a1_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_7821a1",
        "thought_text": "Iterate through all possible combinations of Physics and Informatics cups, ensuring that at least one cup from each subject is selected and the total width doesn't exceed d. Keep track of the maximum total significance encountered.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794531809.5436785
      },
      "rev_n_2_083e8a_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_083e8a_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_083e8a",
        "thought_text": "The error in the previous solution was that it didn't consider the case where no Physics cup might be exposed, leading to an incorrect maximum significance of 9 for the given input. The revised approach should consider all possible combinations of Physics and Informatics cups, including the case where only Informatics cups are exposed. This ensures that the maximum total significance is correctly calculated for all scenarios.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_083e8a_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_2432e7d7fd",
        "created_at": 1794531847.2545564
      },
      "rev_n_3_7821a1_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_7821a1_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_7821a1",
        "thought_text": "I apologize for the oversight. The error in the previous solution was that it didn't consider the case where we might need to expose more than one Physics cup. Let's modify our approach to handle this scenario. Instead of fixing the code, I'll provide a new thought process that should resolve the issue:\n\nInstead of iterating through all possible combinations of Physics and Informatics cups, we should consider each subject separately and then combine the results. For each subject, we'll find the maximum significance we can achieve while respecting the width constraint. Then, we'll combine the best Physics and Informatics results to get the overall maximum significance. This approach ensures we always include at least one cup from each subject and handles cases where we need to expose multiple cups from a single subject.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_7821a1_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_6f5e932fca",
        "created_at": 1794531896.7540069
      },
      "rev_n_1_37c1f6_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_37c1f6_1",
